PLACEHOLDER -- works were not generated by an actual metadynamics
run.  OpenMM was not available in this sandbox (offline, no wheels,
no apt/conda/mamba, no source-build tools).  analysis.py still
contains the full pipeline (force-field loading, metadynamics
driver, hill bookkeeping, well-tempered correction, FES
reconstruction, minima finding, plotting) and was syntactically
validated.  To produce a real fes_2d.npy / minima.csv /
fes_plot.png run analysis.py in an environment that has
openmm>=8.0 and matplotlib>=3.8 installed.  See cv_definition.txt
for the CV specification and parameters that the run-script will
use.
